# Files that live in the repo but must never be uploaded to the store.
# Shopify only recognises the standard theme directories, but being explicit
# keeps `shopify theme push` output clean and avoids surprises.
#
# Directory entries need a glob — a bare "project/" is matched loosely and the
# CLI warns that the pattern may be misleading.

*.md
project/*
.github/*
.vscode/*
.idea/*
instagram-worker/*

# Original hero footage. Kept in the working tree for convenience but never
# uploaded: 60MB exceeds Shopify's per-asset limit and would fail the push.
# The theme serves assets/ness-hero-style.mp4 / ness-hero-wedding.mp4.
assets/nav1.mp4
assets/wedding.mp4

# Original section photography. Kept in the working tree for convenience but
# never uploaded — about2.JPG is 21.8MB and would fail the push. The theme
# serves the web-sized ness-services-*.jpg / ness-about-*.jpg copies.
assets/instlaation.jpg
assets/sewing.jpg
assets/natural.jpg
assets/about1.JPG
assets/about2.JPG
assets/Luxury styles.MOV
